IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 10A (ONLINE COMMUNICATION SERVICE REGULATION), Division 1 (scope and key concepts, ss 45A to 45D) and Division 2 (offences involving egregious content, ss 45E to 45J).
-- Part 10A entered with Act 38 of 2022 (wef 1 February 2023); these rules state the 2024 consolidation and the seat layer gates by date.
-- Section 45A is a purpose clause that creates no rule (inert, reason 1). "Singapore end-user link" is defined in s 45T (module sgba-p10a-d4.l4); here it is a plain fact.

§ `45B. Application`

-- src:2747 | 45B. This Part applies to and in relation to any content that is
-- src:2748 | provided on any online communication service and is accessible by
-- src:2749 | any Singapore end-user except that if the content was published on
-- src:2750 | the Internet before the date of commencement of section 5 of the
-- src:2751 | Online Safety (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2022, this Part does
-- src:2752 | not apply to the content on an online communication service unless
-- src:2753 | the content remains accessible to a Singapore end-user of the service
-- src:2754 | on or after that date.
@ref s 45B (src:2747-2754)
GIVEN `the content is provided on an online communication service and is accessible by a Singapore end-user` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the content was published on the Internet before the commencement of section 5 of the Online Safety (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the content remains accessible to a Singapore end-user of the service on or after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45B this Part applies to the content` MEANS
    `the content is provided on an online communication service and is accessible by a Singapore end-user` AND ((NOT `the content was published on the Internet before the commencement of section 5 of the Online Safety (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2022`) OR `the content remains accessible to a Singapore end-user of the service on or after that date`)

§ `45C. When content is provided or communicated on online communication service`

-- src:2761 | 45C.—(1) For the purposes of this Part, content is provided on an
-- src:2762 | online communication service if the content can be accessed by one
-- src:2763 | or more of the end-users using the service.
@ref s 45C(1) (src:2761-2763)
GIVEN `the content can be accessed by one or more of the end-users using the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45C(1) the content is provided on the online communication service` MEANS
    `the content can be accessed by one or more of the end-users using the service`

-- src:2765 | (2) For the purposes of this Part, content is communicated on an
-- src:2766 | online communication service by an end-user if the end-user causes
-- src:2767 | the content to be accessible by one or more other end-users using the
-- src:2768 | service.
@ref s 45C(2) (src:2765-2768)
GIVEN `the end-user causes the content to be accessible by one or more other end-users using the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45C(2) the content is communicated on the online communication service by the end-user` MEANS
    `the end-user causes the content to be accessible by one or more other end-users using the service`

§ `45D. Meaning of "egregious content"`

-- src:2777 | 45D.—(1) In this Part, “egregious content” means —
-- src:2779 | (a) content that advocates or instructs on suicide or self-harm;
-- src:2781 | (b) content that advocates or instructs on violence or cruelty
-- src:2782 | to, physical abuse of, or acts of torture or other infliction of
-- src:2783 | serious physical harm on, human beings;
-- src:2785 | (c) content that advocates or instructs on sexual violence or
-- src:2786 | coercion in association with sexual conduct, whether or not
-- src:2787 | involving the commission of a heinous sex crime;
-- src:2789 | (d) content depicting for a sexual purpose, or that exploits, the
-- src:2790 | nudity of a child or part of a child in a way that reasonable
-- src:2791 | persons would regard as being offensive, whether or not
-- src:2792 | sexual activity is involved;
-- src:2794 | (e) content that advocates engaging in conduct in a way that —
-- src:2796 | (i) obstructs or is likely to obstruct any public health
-- src:2797 | measure carried out in Singapore; or
-- src:2799 | (ii) results or is likely to result in a public health risk in
-- src:2800 | Singapore;
-- src:2802 | (f) content dealing with matters of race or religion in a way
-- src:2803 | that is likely to cause feelings of enmity, hatred, ill will or
-- src:2804 | hostility against, or contempt for or ridicule of, different
-- src:2805 | racial or religious groups in Singapore;
-- src:2807 | (g) content that advocates or instructs on terrorism; or
-- src:2809 | (h) any other content that is prescribed by Part 10A regulations
-- src:2810 | as egregious content.
@ref s 45D(1)(a) to (h) (src:2777-2810)
GIVEN `it advocates or instructs on suicide or self-harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it advocates or instructs on violence or cruelty to, physical abuse of, or acts of torture or other infliction of serious physical harm on, human beings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it advocates or instructs on sexual violence or coercion in association with sexual conduct, whether or not involving a heinous sex crime` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it depicts for a sexual purpose, or exploits, the nudity of a child or part of a child in a way reasonable persons would regard as offensive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it advocates engaging in conduct that obstructs or is likely to obstruct a public health measure carried out in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it advocates engaging in conduct that results or is likely to result in a public health risk in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it deals with matters of race or religion in a way likely to cause enmity, hatred, ill will or hostility against, or contempt for or ridicule of, different racial or religious groups in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it advocates or instructs on terrorism` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is other content prescribed by Part 10A regulations as egregious content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45D(1) the content is egregious content` MEANS
    `it advocates or instructs on suicide or self-harm`
    OR `it advocates or instructs on violence or cruelty to, physical abuse of, or acts of torture or other infliction of serious physical harm on, human beings`
    OR `it advocates or instructs on sexual violence or coercion in association with sexual conduct, whether or not involving a heinous sex crime`
    OR `it depicts for a sexual purpose, or exploits, the nudity of a child or part of a child in a way reasonable persons would regard as offensive`
    OR `it advocates engaging in conduct that obstructs or is likely to obstruct a public health measure carried out in Singapore`
    OR `it advocates engaging in conduct that results or is likely to result in a public health risk in Singapore`
    OR `it deals with matters of race or religion in a way likely to cause enmity, hatred, ill will or hostility against, or contempt for or ridicule of, different racial or religious groups in Singapore`
    OR `it advocates or instructs on terrorism`
    OR `it is other content prescribed by Part 10A regulations as egregious content`

-- src:2812 | (2) It does not matter if the content in subsection (1) relates to
-- src:2813 | conduct engaged in within or outside Singapore.
@ref s 45D(2) (src:2812-2813)
GIVEN `the content relates to conduct engaged in outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45D(2) it matters whether the conduct is within or outside Singapore` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:2815 | (3) In this section —
-- src:2817 | “heinous sex crime” means —
-- src:2819 | (a) an offence under the Penal Code 1871 involving
-- src:2820 | serious sexual assault such as rape or sexual assault
-- src:2825 | by penetration, or sexual communication with or
-- src:2826 | sexual grooming of a child;
-- src:2828 | (b) an offence under section 8 of the Children and Young
-- src:2829 | Persons Act 1993;
-- src:2831 | (c) an abetment of or a conspiracy to commit an offence
-- src:2832 | specified in paragraph (a) or (b);
-- src:2834 | (d) an attempt to commit an offence specified in
-- src:2835 | paragraph (a) or (b); or
-- src:2837 | (e) conduct outside Singapore which, had it been
-- src:2838 | engaged in within Singapore, would have been an
-- src:2839 | offence specified in paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d) and
-- src:2840 | punishable by a Singapore court;
@ref s 45D(3) chapeau and "heinous sex crime" (src:2815-2840)
GIVEN `it is an offence under the Penal Code 1871 involving serious sexual assault such as rape or sexual assault by penetration, or sexual communication with or sexual grooming of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an offence under section 8 of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an abetment of, a conspiracy to commit, or an attempt to commit, an offence of those kinds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conduct outside Singapore which, had it been engaged in within Singapore, would have been such an offence and punishable by a Singapore court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45D(3) the conduct is a heinous sex crime` MEANS
    `it is an offence under the Penal Code 1871 involving serious sexual assault such as rape or sexual assault by penetration, or sexual communication with or sexual grooming of a child`
    OR `it is an offence under section 8 of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993`
    OR `it is an abetment of, a conspiracy to commit, or an attempt to commit, an offence of those kinds`
    OR `it is conduct outside Singapore which, had it been engaged in within Singapore, would have been such an offence and punishable by a Singapore court`

-- src:2842 | “public health measure” means the organised response by
-- src:2843 | society (including Government) to prevent, mitigate or
-- src:2844 | control a public health risk;
@ref s 45D(3) "public health measure" (src:2842-2844)
GIVEN `it is the organised response by society (including Government) to prevent, mitigate or control a public health risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45D(3) the response is a public health measure` MEANS
    `it is the organised response by society (including Government) to prevent, mitigate or control a public health risk`

-- src:2846 | “public health risk” means circumstances, a thing or substance
-- src:2847 | that —
-- src:2849 | (a) is or is likely to be hazardous to the health of
-- src:2850 | individuals in the context of the wider health of the
-- src:2851 | community; or
-- src:2853 | (b) contributes or is likely to contribute to disease or the
-- src:2854 | transmission of an infectious disease to or among
-- src:2855 | human beings;
@ref s 45D(3) "public health risk" (src:2846-2855)
GIVEN `it is hazardous or likely to be hazardous to the health of individuals in the context of the wider health of the community` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contributes or is likely to contribute to disease or the transmission of an infectious disease to or among human beings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45D(3) the circumstances, thing or substance is a public health risk` MEANS
    `it is hazardous or likely to be hazardous to the health of individuals in the context of the wider health of the community` OR `it contributes or is likely to contribute to disease or the transmission of an infectious disease to or among human beings`

-- src:2857 | “terrorism” means the engaging in any conduct constituting —
-- src:2859 | (a) a terrorist act within the meaning given by
-- src:2860 | section 2(2) and (3) of the Terrorism (Suppression
-- src:2861 | of Financing) Act 2002 affecting persons or property
-- src:2862 | situated in Singapore;
-- src:2864 | (b) a terrorist bombing offence within the meaning given
-- src:2865 | by section 2 of the Terrorism (Suppression of
-- src:2866 | Bombings) Act 2007;
-- src:2871 | (c) a nuclear terrorism offence within the meaning given
-- src:2872 | by section 2 of the Terrorism (Suppression of Misuse
-- src:2873 | of Radioactive Material) Act 2017;
-- src:2875 | (d) an abetment of or a conspiracy to commit an act or
-- src:2876 | offence specified in paragraph (a), (b) or (c);
-- src:2878 | (e) an attempt to commit an act or offence specified in
-- src:2879 | paragraph (a), (b) or (c); or
-- src:2881 | (f) an offence specified in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or
-- src:2882 | (e) and punishable by a Singapore court if the
-- src:2883 | conduct had been engaged in within Singapore.
@ref s 45D(3) "terrorism" (src:2857-2883)
GIVEN `it is a terrorist act within the meaning of section 2(2) and (3) of the Terrorism (Suppression of Financing) Act 2002 affecting persons or property situated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a terrorist bombing offence within the meaning of section 2 of the Terrorism (Suppression of Bombings) Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a nuclear terrorism offence within the meaning of section 2 of the Terrorism (Suppression of Misuse of Radioactive Material) Act 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an abetment of, conspiracy to commit, or attempt to commit, an act or offence of those kinds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is such an offence punishable by a Singapore court if the conduct had been engaged in within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45D(3) the conduct is terrorism` MEANS
    `it is a terrorist act within the meaning of section 2(2) and (3) of the Terrorism (Suppression of Financing) Act 2002 affecting persons or property situated in Singapore`
    OR `it is a terrorist bombing offence within the meaning of section 2 of the Terrorism (Suppression of Bombings) Act 2007`
    OR `it is a nuclear terrorism offence within the meaning of section 2 of the Terrorism (Suppression of Misuse of Radioactive Material) Act 2017`
    OR `it is an abetment of, conspiracy to commit, or attempt to commit, an act or offence of those kinds`
    OR `it is such an offence punishable by a Singapore court if the conduct had been engaged in within Singapore`

§ `45E. Offence of not stopping egregious content on online communication service`

-- src:2892 | 45E.—(1) A person commits an offence if —
-- src:2894 | (a) the person provides an online communication service with
-- src:2895 | a Singapore end-user link;
-- src:2897 | (b) the online communication service provides or can be used
-- src:2898 | to access content on the online communication service;
-- src:2900 | (c) the content is egregious content;
-- src:2902 | (d) the person knows, or ought reasonably to know that —
-- src:2904 | (i) the online communication service provides or can be
-- src:2905 | used to access that content; and
-- src:2907 | (ii) the content is egregious content; and
-- src:2909 | (e) the person fails in the person’s duty under section 45J to
-- src:2910 | comply with a section 45H direction given to the person in
-- src:2911 | relation to that egregious content provided on that online
-- src:2912 | communication service by the person.
@ref s 45E(1) (src:2892-2912)
GIVEN `the person provides an online communication service with a Singapore end-user link` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service provides or can be used to access content on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the content is egregious content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the service provides or can be used to access that content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the content is egregious content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails in the duty under section 45J to comply with a section 45H direction given in relation to that egregious content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45E(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    `the person provides an online communication service with a Singapore end-user link` AND `the service provides or can be used to access content on it` AND `the content is egregious content` AND `the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the service provides or can be used to access that content` AND `the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the content is egregious content` AND `the person fails in the duty under section 45J to comply with a section 45H direction given in relation to that egregious content`

-- src:2914 | (2) A person that is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall
-- src:2915 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1 million and, in the
-- src:2916 | case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $100,000
-- src:2921 | for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:2922 | conviction.
@ref s 45E(2) (src:2914-2922)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 45E(2) the punishment on conviction` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `fine not exceeding` IS 1000000
                  , `imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is provided`
                  , `daily fine` IS `a further fine not exceeding, per day or part of a day after conviction` 100000
                  , `forfeiture` IS `no forfeiture is provided`

-- src:2924 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), it is immaterial whether the
-- src:2925 | online communication service is provided from outside Singapore or
-- src:2926 | provided in or from Singapore.
@ref s 45E(3) (src:2924-2926)
GIVEN `the service is provided from outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45E(3) it matters whether the service is provided from outside Singapore or in or from Singapore` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:2928 | (4) If —
-- src:2930 | (a) a section 45H direction is given in relation to an online
-- src:2931 | communication service provided by a person; and
-- src:2933 | (b) in a prosecution of the person for an offence against
-- src:2934 | subsection (1), it is proven that the online communication
-- src:2935 | service provides or can be used to, at the time the direction
-- src:2936 | was given, access the content specified in the direction,
-- src:2938 | then, in that prosecution, it must be presumed until the contrary is
-- src:2939 | proved, that the person knew —
-- src:2941 | (c) that the online communication service provides or can be
-- src:2942 | used to access that content at the time the direction was
-- src:2943 | given; and
-- src:2945 | (d) that the content is egregious content at the time the
-- src:2946 | direction was given.
@ref s 45E(4) (src:2928-2946)
GIVEN `a section 45H direction is given in relation to the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proven that the service provides or can be used to access, at the time of the direction, the content the direction specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45E(4) it is presumed until the contrary is proved that the person knew the service provided access to that content and that the content was egregious content, at the time of the direction` MEANS
    IF `a section 45H direction is given in relation to the service` AND `it is proven that the service provides or can be used to access, at the time of the direction, the content the direction specifies` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `45F. Offence of not stopping access to online communication service`

-- src:2952 | 45F.—(1) A person commits an offence if —
-- src:2954 | (a) the person provides an internet access service with a
-- src:2955 | Singapore end-user link;
-- src:2957 | (b) the internet access service can be used by a Singapore end-
-- src:2958 | user of an online communication service to access content
-- src:2959 | provided on the online communication service;
-- src:2961 | (c) the content is egregious content;
-- src:2963 | (d) the person knows, or ought reasonably to know that —
-- src:2965 | (i) the internet access service can be used by a
-- src:2966 | Singapore end-user of the online communication
-- src:2971 | service to access the content provided on the online
-- src:2972 | communication service; and
-- src:2974 | (ii) the content is egregious content; and
-- src:2976 | (e) the person fails in the person’s duty under section 45J to
-- src:2977 | comply with a section 45I blocking direction given to the
-- src:2978 | person in relation to access to the online communication
-- src:2979 | service through its internet access service.
@ref s 45F(1) (src:2952-2979)
GIVEN `the person provides an internet access service with a Singapore end-user link` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the internet access service can be used by a Singapore end-user of an online communication service to access content provided on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the content is egregious content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the internet access service can be so used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the content is egregious content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails in the duty under section 45J to comply with a section 45I blocking direction given in relation to access to the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45F(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    `the person provides an internet access service with a Singapore end-user link` AND `the internet access service can be used by a Singapore end-user of an online communication service to access content provided on it` AND `the content is egregious content` AND `the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the internet access service can be so used` AND `the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, that the content is egregious content` AND `the person fails in the duty under section 45J to comply with a section 45I blocking direction given in relation to access to the service`

-- src:2981 | (2) A person that is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall
-- src:2982 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $20,000 for each day
-- src:2983 | or part of a day the person does not comply with a section 45I
-- src:2984 | blocking direction given to the person but not exceeding a total fine of
-- src:2985 | $500,000.
@ref s 45F(2) (src:2981-2985)
-- A fine of up to $20,000 for each day or part of a day of non-compliance, but not exceeding a total of $500,000.
GIVEN `the number of days or parts of a day the person does not comply with the section 45I blocking direction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 45F(2) the most the person can be fined in total` MEANS
    IF `the number of days or parts of a day the person does not comply with the section 45I blocking direction` TIMES 20000 AT MOST 500000 THEN `the number of days or parts of a day the person does not comply with the section 45I blocking direction` TIMES 20000 ELSE 500000

-- src:2987 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), it is immaterial whether the
-- src:2988 | online communication service is provided from outside Singapore or
-- src:2989 | provided in or from Singapore.
@ref s 45F(3) (src:2987-2989)
GIVEN `the service is provided from outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45F(3) it matters whether the service is provided from outside Singapore or in or from Singapore` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:2991 | (4) If —
-- src:2993 | (a) a section 45I blocking direction is given in relation to an
-- src:2994 | internet access service provided by a person; and
-- src:2996 | (b) in a prosecution of the person for an offence against
-- src:2997 | subsection (1), it is proven that the internet access service
-- src:2998 | can, at the time the direction was given, be used by a
-- src:2999 | Singapore end-user of an online communication service to
-- src:3000 | access content provided on the online communication
-- src:3001 | service using the internet access service specified in the
-- src:3002 | direction,
-- src:3004 | then, in that prosecution, it must be presumed until the contrary is
-- src:3005 | proved that the person knew —
-- src:3007 | (c) that the internet access service can, at the time the direction
-- src:3008 | was given, be used by a Singapore end-user of the online
-- src:3009 | communication service to access content provided on that
-- src:3010 | online communication service; and
-- src:3012 | (d) that the content is egregious content at the time the
-- src:3013 | direction was given.
@ref s 45F(4) (src:2991-3013)
GIVEN `a section 45I blocking direction is given in relation to the internet access service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proven that the internet access service can, at the time of the direction, be used by a Singapore end-user of the online communication service to access content provided on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45F(4) it is presumed until the contrary is proved that the person knew that access was possible and that the content was egregious content, at the time of the direction` MEANS
    IF `a section 45I blocking direction is given in relation to the internet access service` AND `it is proven that the internet access service can, at the time of the direction, be used by a Singapore end-user of the online communication service to access content provided on it` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `45G. Defence`

-- src:3022 | 45G. In a prosecution of the person for an offence against
-- src:3023 | section 45E(1) or 45F(1), it is a defence for the person charged to
-- src:3024 | prove, on a balance of probabilities, that —
-- src:3026 | (a) it was not reasonably practicable to do more than what was
-- src:3027 | in fact done to satisfy the duty in section 45J; and
-- src:3029 | (b) there was no better practicable means than was in fact used
-- src:3030 | to satisfy the duty in section 45J.
@ref s 45G (src:3022-3030)
GIVEN `the person proves on a balance of probabilities that it was not reasonably practicable to do more than what was in fact done to satisfy the duty in section 45J` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves on a balance of probabilities that there was no better practicable means than was in fact used to satisfy the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45G the person has the defence` MEANS
    `the person proves on a balance of probabilities that it was not reasonably practicable to do more than what was in fact done to satisfy the duty in section 45J` AND `the person proves on a balance of probabilities that there was no better practicable means than was in fact used to satisfy the duty`

§ `45H. Section 45H direction`

-- src:3036 | 45H.—(1) If the Authority is satisfied that —
-- src:3038 | (a) any egregious content is being provided on an online
-- src:3039 | communication service with a Singapore end-user link;
-- src:3040 | and
-- src:3042 | (b) Singapore end-users of the service can access the
-- src:3043 | egregious content,
@ref s 45H(1)(a) and (b) (src:3036-3043)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that egregious content is being provided on an online communication service with a Singapore end-user link` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that Singapore end-users of the service can access the egregious content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45H(1) the Authority may give the provider a written direction` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied that egregious content is being provided on an online communication service with a Singapore end-user link` AND `the Authority is satisfied that Singapore end-users of the service can access the egregious content`

-- src:3045 | the Authority may give the provider of the online communication
-- src:3046 | service a written direction requiring the provider —
-- src:3048 | (c) to do one or more of the following as the Authority
-- src:3049 | considers appropriate:
-- src:3051 | (i) to disable access to the egregious content on its
-- src:3052 | service by Singapore end-users who use or may use
-- src:3053 | the service;
-- src:3055 | (ii) to stop delivery or communication of content to an
-- src:3056 | account or accounts of —
-- src:3058 | (A) all Singapore end-users of the service; or
-- src:3060 | (B) any particular group of end-users comprising
-- src:3061 | one or more Singapore end-users of the
-- src:3062 | service,
-- src:3064 | (ii) so as to stop or reduce the communication, provision
-- src:3065 | or access, or further communication, provision or
-- src:3070 | access, by Singapore end-users of egregious content
-- src:3071 | on the online communication service; and
-- src:3073 | (d) to do so within the period specified in the written direction,
-- src:3074 | or any extension of that period that the Authority may
-- src:3075 | allow in any particular case.
@ref s 45H(1)(c) and (d) (src:3045-3075)
-- READING (fork F-BA-07): the closing words "so as to stop or reduce the communication, provision or access ... of egregious content on the online communication service" are printed as a paragraph lettered (ii).
-- Read as the end of paragraph (c)(ii) only, they qualify the stopping of delivery or communication to accounts (reading A, encoded below).
-- Read as the end of the whole of paragraph (c), they qualify disabling access as well (reading B, not encoded: it adds the same purpose to the first limb).
GIVEN `it requires the provider to disable access to the egregious content by Singapore end-users who use or may use the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires the provider to stop delivery or communication of content to the account or accounts of all Singapore end-users, or of a particular group of one or more of them, so as to stop or reduce communication, provision or access by Singapore end-users of egregious content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it requires the provider to do so within the period specified in the written direction, or any extension the Authority allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45H(1) the direction is of a kind the subsection allows` MEANS
    (`it requires the provider to disable access to the egregious content by Singapore end-users who use or may use the service` OR `it requires the provider to stop delivery or communication of content to the account or accounts of all Singapore end-users, or of a particular group of one or more of them, so as to stop or reduce communication, provision or access by Singapore end-users of egregious content`) AND `it requires the provider to do so within the period specified in the written direction, or any extension the Authority allows`

-- src:3077 | (2) To avoid doubt, a requirement in subsection (1)(c)(ii) —
-- src:3079 | (a) may include requiring altering, terminating or suspending
-- src:3080 | any functionality of the service provided to the Singapore
-- src:3081 | end-user concerned; but
-- src:3083 | (b) must not require the doing of any thing with respect to the
-- src:3084 | provision of an online communication service to the whole
-- src:3085 | or part of any area in Singapore.
@ref s 45H(2) (src:3077-3085)
GIVEN `the requirement is to alter, terminate or suspend a functionality of the service provided to the Singapore end-user concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is to do something with respect to the provision of an online communication service to the whole or part of an area in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45H(2) a requirement under subsection (1)(c)(ii) may include this` MEANS
    `the requirement is to alter, terminate or suspend a functionality of the service provided to the Singapore end-user concerned` AND (NOT `the requirement is to do something with respect to the provision of an online communication service to the whole or part of an area in Singapore`)

-- src:3087 | (3) In addition, a requirement in subsection (1)(c) must not relate to
-- src:3088 | any user-generated content that is communication between 2 or more
-- src:3089 | end-users that is of a private or domestic nature.
@ref s 45H(3) (src:3087-3089)
GIVEN `the requirement relates to user-generated content that is communication between 2 or more end-users of a private or domestic nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45H(3) a requirement under subsection (1)(c) may relate to it` MEANS
    NOT `the requirement relates to user-generated content that is communication between 2 or more end-users of a private or domestic nature`

-- src:3091 | (4) The egregious content must be, so far as is reasonably
-- src:3092 | practicable, identified by the Authority in a section 45H direction
-- src:3093 | in a way that is sufficient to enable the provider concerned to comply
-- src:3094 | with the direction.
@ref s 45H(4) (src:3091-3094)
GIVEN `the Authority identified the egregious content, so far as reasonably practicable, in a way sufficient to enable the provider to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45H(4) the direction identifies the egregious content as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the Authority identified the egregious content, so far as reasonably practicable, in a way sufficient to enable the provider to comply`

-- src:3096 | (5) In this section, “account” includes —
-- src:3098 | (a) a free account;
-- src:3100 | (b) a prepaid account; and
-- src:3102 | (c) anything that may reasonably be regarded as the equivalent
-- src:3103 | of an account.
@ref s 45H(5) "account" (src:3096-3103)
GIVEN `it is a free account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a prepaid account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it may reasonably be regarded as the equivalent of an account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45H(5) account includes this` MEANS
    IF `it is a free account` OR `it is a prepaid account` OR `it may reasonably be regarded as the equivalent of an account` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `45I. Section 45I blocking direction`

-- src:3109 | 45I.—(1) This section applies to a provider of an internet access
-- src:3110 | service.
@ref s 45I(1) (src:3109-3110)
GIVEN `the person is a provider of an internet access service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45I(1) section 45I applies to the person` MEANS `the person is a provider of an internet access service`

-- src:3112 | (2) If the Authority is satisfied that —
-- src:3114 | (a) a provider of an online communication service with a
-- src:3115 | Singapore end-user link which is given a section 45H
-- src:3116 | direction fails to comply with the direction; and
-- src:3121 | (b) the internet access service has control over access by
-- src:3122 | Singapore end-users of the online communication service
-- src:3123 | to content provided on that online communication service,
-- src:3125 | the Authority may direct the provider of the internet access service to
-- src:3126 | stop access by Singapore end-users to the online communication
-- src:3127 | service.
@ref s 45I(2) (src:3112-3127)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that a provider of an online communication service with a Singapore end-user link, given a section 45H direction, fails to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the internet access service has control over access by Singapore end-users of the online communication service to content provided on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 45I(2) the Authority may direct the internet access provider to stop access by Singapore end-users to the online communication service` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied that a provider of an online communication service with a Singapore end-user link, given a section 45H direction, fails to comply with it` AND `the Authority is satisfied that the internet access service has control over access by Singapore end-users of the online communication service to content provided on it`

§ `45J. Duty to comply`

-- src:3133 | 45J.—(1) Every provider of an online communication service or an
-- src:3134 | internet access service to whom is given a section 45H direction or
-- src:3135 | section 45I blocking direction, has the duty to take all reasonably
-- src:3136 | practicable steps to comply with the direction given to the provider.
@ref s 45J(1) (src:3133-3136)
GIVEN `the provider is given a section 45H direction or a section 45I blocking direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider took all reasonably practicable steps to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45J(1) the provider has done its duty` MEANS
    IF `the provider is given a section 45H direction or a section 45I blocking direction` THEN JUST `the provider took all reasonably practicable steps to comply` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3138 | (2) No civil or criminal liability is incurred by a provider of an
-- src:3139 | online communication service or an internet access service provider,
-- src:3140 | or an officer, employee or agent of such a provider, for anything done
-- src:3141 | or omitted to be done with reasonable care and in good faith in
-- src:3142 | complying with a section 45H direction or section 45I blocking
-- src:3143 | direction given to the provider.
@ref s 45J(2) (src:3138-3143)
GIVEN `the thing was done or omitted with reasonable care and in good faith in complying with a section 45H direction or section 45I blocking direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45J(2) the provider, or its officer, employee or agent, incurs civil or criminal liability for it` MEANS
    IF `the thing was done or omitted with reasonable care and in good faith in complying with a section 45H direction or section 45I blocking direction` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
